+CrDK remains pinned at b6c3335136b7f6b28271917de11e8f11982975fc, available on Project-Aloha/CrDK backup/2610. The upstream CrDK checkout and the packer remain unchanged. The Canoe splash extension lives in kShimC's existing ports/crdk patch, which introduces DisplayLib; that library does not exist at the pinned upstream CrDK revision.
 
 Remaining board work:
 - Confirm actual key reads and firmware-granted SPMI/MMIO access on hardware.
-- Adapt continuous-splash discovery to the board's SDE/HFI resources. The current stock tree exposes more pipe/mixer slots than the existing reader accepts.
+- Validate inherited scanout, framebuffer format and firmware-granted display access on hardware. The offline Canoe reader does not initialize the panel or DSI.
 - Add Novatek SPI touch support if required for the boot menu; FTM4/FTM5 are not substitutes.
