--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/runtime-memory-handoff.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+Runtime RAM handoff and TB323FU diagnostic profile (2026-10-03)
+
+configs/tb323fu_defconfig enables framebuffer/LVGL and Qualcomm volume/power keys, disables touch, SMP workers and the borrowed UEFI test menu. It is a first-hardware-test profile, not proof of TB323FU support.
+
+For a Linux manifest entry with a separate DTB, the zero-length /chosen/kshim,inherit-runtime-memory property opts into dt_handoff_memory. Unmarked payloads retain their existing behavior. The source is the bootloader runtime DT; the destination is a copy of the payload DT in a 256 KiB, 8-byte-aligned static buffer. Root RAM banks are normalized to destination 2/2 cells. Source reservations are conservatively reconciled without copying Android hardware bindings, phandles or bootargs. Existing destination reservations remain; source no-map intervals are added only for uncovered gaps. Conflicts with mapped/reusable destination areas fail rather than weaken reservation semantics. Missing, empty, malformed, overflowing or overlapping source RAM fails.
+
+The first Linux profile requires a built-in initramfs. Destination linux,initrd-start/end are removed; Android initrd addresses are not imported. A malformed opt-in or handoff failure returns to the original base kernel and original runtime DT. CrDK pin and Manifest ABI are unchanged.
+
+Validation on build-server Docker: 18/18 ASan/UBSan host tests; ARM64 build within the 4 MiB slot with no undefined symbols; 8/8 manifest QEMU cases; tests/linux_handoff_qemu.py passes actual Linux boot into an embedded diagnostic PID1 and rejection/fallback. The Linux test accepts explicit runtime/kernel/packer/base/out paths; base is the existing manifest_qemu.py A.bin fixture. It does not build or contact hardware.
+
+The diagnostic kernel used the Kaanapali source commit 37a76066478cadff757c8dcf7cb3fde58d5c5e58 (7.2.0-rc5). The TB323FU DTS and diagnostic initramfs sources are retained outside this repository in the task's mainline-bringup directory. A synthetic-RAM fixture is only test evidence, never a device DT.
+
+Remaining hardware boundary: actual display format/address, MMIO permission, PMIC key access, bootloader runtime memory layout, Android return and unsigned boot image acceptance. QEMU does not validate these. No hardware was accessed. No new PR or remote push accompanies this local change.
